FP64 libm transcriptions -- Arm optimized-routines and CORE-MATH

The UW moist-turbulence boundary layer computes in binary64 and is graded
bit for bit against a gfortran/glibc build of WRF, so it carries its own
binary64 libm rather than calling CUDA's: gpuwm/core/kernels/glibc_flt64.cuh,
prepended to uwpbl.cu by the kernel loader. The header opens with its
